  "notes": "Modified cash basis village (basis recorded as cash). Governmental lines from the Total column of the governmental funds statement (p4); business-type from the proprietary statement Total column (p6). Fund balance roll-forward: 838,258 + 763,413 - 727,651 = 874,020. Cash fields: governmental funds 'Cash and cash equivalents' line (p3, 2023 and 2022 Total columns); CDs as investments; restricted cash and county treasurer cash are separate lines in the balance sheet. Business-type: 503,967 + 287,052 - 261,737 = 529,282. Balance sheet: governmental lines from p3 (totals equal p1 governmental 874,020; p3 prints Restricted for Community development 1,155 where p1 splits community improvement 1,153 / community development 2), business-type from p1. Detail: General Fund combining schedule by department (pp8-9); utility funds have no own schedules, so their statement-column lines are not added (as FY2024, user rule 2026-10-28). The all-funds budget schedule (p7) prints only broad Taxes/Federal/State/Local groups for all funds combined and is not recorded; the Streets Fund has no own schedule. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
}
